  "question": {
    "text": "In the reaction of formation of sulphur trioxide by contact process $2 \\mathrm{SO}_2+\\mathrm{O}_2 \\rightleftharpoons 2 \\mathrm{SO}_3$ the rate of reaction was measured as\n$\\frac{\\mathrm{d}\\left[\\mathrm{O}_2\\right]}{\\mathrm{dt}}=-2.5 \\times 10^{-4} \\mathrm{~mol} \\mathrm{~L}^{-1} \\mathrm{~s}^{-1}$. The rate of reaction is terms of $\\left[\\mathrm{SO}_2\\right]$ in $\\mathrm{mol} \\mathrm{L}^{-1} \\mathrm{~s}^{-1}$ will be:"
  },
  "options": [
    {
      "text": "\n$-1.25 \\times 10^{-4}$\n",
      "is_correct": false
    },
    {
      "text": "\n$-2.50 \\times 10^{-4}$\n",
      "is_correct": false
    },
    {
      "text": "\n$-3.75 \\times 10^{-4}$\n",
      "is_correct": false
    },
    {
      "text": "\n$-5.00 \\times 10^{-4}$",
      "is_correct": true
    }
  ],
  "correct_answer": [
    "D"
  ],
  "solution": {
    "text": "From rate law\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}\n&-\\frac{1}{2} \\frac{\\mathrm{dSO}_2}{\\mathrm{dt}}=-\\frac{\\mathrm{dO}_2}{\\mathrm{dt}}=\\frac{1}{2} \\frac{\\mathrm{dSO}_3}{\\mathrm{dt}} \\\\\n&\\therefore-\\frac{\\mathrm{dSO}_2}{\\mathrm{dt}}=-2 \\times \\frac{\\mathrm{dO}_2}{\\mathrm{dt}} \\\\\n&=-2 \\times 2.5 \\times 10^{-4} \\\\\n&=-5 \\times 10^{-4} \\mathrm{~mol} \\mathrm{~L}^{-1} \\mathrm{~s}^{-1}\n\\end{aligned}\n$$"
  }
}